259
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:42,680
He's here too, huh?

260
00:16:43,820 --> 00:16:44,720
Lucky me!

261
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:49,120
All of you are running too slow!

262
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:51,097
I think you're too fast, actually!

263
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:53,597
I'm supposed to blunder
their treasure first, right?

264
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,917
This is totally different
than our usual battles!

265
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,235
The Roger Pirates are seriously tough!

266
00:16:58,780 --> 00:17:00,520
He's not listening at all!

267
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:07,940
Koyanku!

268
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:21,840
Koyanku! Yes!

269
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,340
He's as strong as they say he is.

270
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:39,600
I think he's wreaked enough
havoc for now. I agree.

271
00:17:40,060 --> 00:17:43,520
Cap 'n, Rayleigh, wait! Huh? Allow me.

272
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,955
I'd sure hate to see my crew get hurt.

273
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:49,020
You just wanna fight him.

274
00:17:52,420 --> 00:17:54,660
I smell a beast.

275
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:57,140
Ahoy there, samurai!

276
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:01,860
Divine Departure!

277
00:18:24,260 --> 00:18:26,220
What in the hell was that?

278
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,380
Sit up, pal.

279
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:32,678
We can't have that.

280
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:45,380
There you are.

281
00:18:58,740 --> 00:19:01,860
I'm not sure what you're doing.

282
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,180
You're looking well, Roger.

283
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:30,140
Good to see you.

284
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:32,598
How many years has it been, Newgate?

285
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:35,300
Too many, I say.

286
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,340
Now hand over all you've got!

287
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:54,580
Let's go!

288
00:19:58,220 --> 00:20:01,600
It is a clash between the
greatest crews of the age.

289
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:10,677
The Roger Pirates versus
the Whitebeard Pirates.

290
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:15,360
The intense battle lasted for
three days and three nights.

291
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:19,600
Time to get serious.

292
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:24,677
Sorry kid, but I'm always serious.

293
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:26,160
Tough break!

294
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:39,380
Ah! Ah!

295
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:42,930
Ah!

296
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:46,130
Ah!

297
00:20:47,060 --> 00:20:47,890
Ah!

298
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:50,920
Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah!

299
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:52,470
Ah! Ah!

300
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:53,810
Ah!

301
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:56,997
How's three boxes of
turkey for one barrel?

302
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:57,910
Good deal!

303
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,560
I like this shirt!

304
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:01,177
Where did you find this one?

305
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,337
Let me have more! Hold it!

306
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:04,277
It took too much!

307
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:06,654
It's got to be an even exchange, buddy.

308
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:08,620
All right, fine.

309
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:12,220
Got something else to fork
over, then? You betcha.

310
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:16,179
Looks like the pillaging
has become a gift exchange.

311
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:22,160
Who are those two? Apprentices?

312
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:28,100
Ah, yeah, they have been
tagging along for a while now.

313
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:30,100
Kind of puny, if you ask me.

314
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:32,880
But look at those faces.

315
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:35,501
They look like hardened old vets.

316
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:39,680
Shanks, look over there. What is it?

317
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:41,340
Do you see that guy?

318
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:45,160
The mean-looking one
with the dumb lid? Yeah.

319
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:50,462
I heard he didn't sleep during the ceasefire
last night or the night before either.

320
00:21:50,780 --> 00:21:51,610
Hmm?

321
00:21:51,693 --> 00:21:52,523
Yeah, so?

322
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,217
Probably just showing off.

323
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:55,182
Are you stupid?

324
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:56,680
It's not normal.

325
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,777
From what I hear, he's never
slept a day in his life.

326
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:00,690
Huh?

327
00:22:00,773 --> 00:22:02,261
Didn't know people could do that.

328
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:03,877
Wow, cool.

329
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:06,040
He must get to have double the fun.

330
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,240
Fun, he says.

331
00:22:07,740 --> 00:22:10,077
Yeah, that guy looks
like a barrel of laughs.

332
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:11,660
He's a monster!

333
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:13,160
You think?

334
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:19,300
So, Odin, can you make
any sense of this text?

335
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:21,700
Indeed, I can read it.

336
00:22:21,860 --> 00:22:24,742
But you must tell me why
you possess this script.

337
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:27,877
Knowledge of these writings
has been passed down from

338
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:31,600
generation to generation
exclusively in the Kozuki clan.

339
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:35,620
It all started 13 years ago.

340
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:40,277
We landed at the destination
of the final Log Pose.

341
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:44,320
And arrived at a place no man
had ever set foot upon before,?

342
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:46,320
Lodestar Island.

343
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:49,220
We disembarked with a smile.

344
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:51,157
But our victory was an empty one!

345
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:54,240
because we learned that it
wasn't the final island.

346
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:59,417
The Log Pose needles were spinning out
of control, refusing to guide us further.

347
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:01,960
That's when it dawned on me!

348
00:23:02,260 --> 00:23:04,160
There was one last destination!

349
00:23:04,760 --> 00:23:06,440
And once I visit there,

350
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:10,900
I will be the first person to
travel the entirety of the world!

351
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:12,940
Look at this.

352
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:15,217
These letters will show me the way.

353
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:19,006
They're rubbings that my crew
and I took from a huge red stone.

354
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:21,677
There are four of those stones out there,

355
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:26,172
and the world government has always
forbidden anyone from deciphering them.

356
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:28,480
They're called pony glyphs, you see.

357
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:32,357
I assumed they were just cultural relics.

358
00:23:32,440 --> 00:23:35,297
But as it turns out,
they're part of a map.

359
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:39,200
That reveals the location of
the last legendary island.

360
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:44,877
Seems odd the government
prohibits us from looking into it.

361
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:47,017
There must be a vast treasure there.

362
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:49,820
How could I possibly resist?

363
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:53,197
The crew who finds it
will become the greatest

364
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:57,460
pirates in the world So let's
get out there, shall we?

365
00:24:03,180 --> 00:24:04,920
The greatest?

366
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:09,320
So, then, we've got a
lot to discuss, don't we?

367
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:26,000
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

368
00:24:29,380 --> 00:24:31,300
I was frozen stiff.

369
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:34,878
For the second time that
day, I found myself stunned.

370
00:24:35,780 --> 00:24:37,640
Who was this fellow?

371
00:24:46,580 --> 00:24:48,600
Believing in old fairy tales now?

372
00:24:48,860 --> 00:24:50,780
You sound like a child, Roger.

373
00:24:57,220 --> 00:25:00,340
But I'm being completely
serious here, Newgate.

374
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:01,910
Please.

375
00:25:03,320 --> 00:25:07,080
Just for one year,
allow me to borrow Odin.

376
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:09,180
It's all that I'm asking.

377
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:11,040
I need that man.

378
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:13,560
With him, I can find the last island.

379
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:18,180
Hey, don't I get a say in any of this!

380
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:20,420
Please, Newgate.

381
00:25:23,060 --> 00:25:24,697
I am begging you.

382
00:25:24,780 --> 00:25:26,700
Captain, what are you doing?

383
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:27,900
Get on your feet!

384
00:25:28,140 --> 00:25:29,022
He's our enemy!

385
00:25:31,560 --> 00:25:33,795
Why would you bow your head like that?

386
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:35,468
Have a bit of dignity, man!

387
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,760
I need you, Odin.

388
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:39,840
You must join us!

389
00:25:39,980 --> 00:25:42,100
I only ask for a year of your time.

390
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:46,360
I Forbidden!

391
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:52,640
Roger, are you trying to
steal my family away from me?

392
00:25:53,560 --> 00:25:56,760
I felt a bolt of excitement
shoot down my spine.

393
00:25:57,500 --> 00:26:00,676
Why is it that only the
Kozuki can read those letters?

394
00:26:01,540 --> 00:26:04,600
Was it fate that brought
me together with this man?

395
00:26:12,180 --> 00:26:16,460
Before I knew it, the words were
leaving my mouth without restraint.

396
00:26:17,340 --> 00:26:20,360
Please, White Kashi, I want to go.

397
00:26:20,980 --> 00:26:22,980
Will you please permit me?

398
00:26:23,640 --> 00:26:27,220
It would be a dream to see
the last island for myself.

399
00:26:31,620 --> 00:26:32,637
He's annoyed.

400
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:35,257
Of course I'm annoyed, you idiot!

401
00:26:35,340 --> 00:26:36,920
How can you do this?

402
00:26:37,020 --> 00:26:41,060
We're practically like brothers It
will only be a year, White Kashi.

403
00:26:49,780 --> 00:26:50,980
I beg you!

404
00:26:55,380 --> 00:26:57,137
You better take care of yourself.

405
00:26:57,220 --> 00:26:58,180
I shall.

406
00:26:59,240 --> 00:27:01,240
We're going to stay with the crew.

407
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:04,037
We've grown quite fond of this ship.

408
00:27:04,120 --> 00:27:07,060
But we'll be waiting for you, won't we?

409
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:15,177
Hmm do as you please your full-fledged

410
00:27:15,260 --> 00:27:19,460
pirates now after all
it's your choice to make

411
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:28,860
He's leaving pops aren't
you gonna send him off

412
00:27:31,980 --> 00:27:34,957
Roger left behind all his
ship's cargo as a thank you

413
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:39,100
this stuff is worth a fortune
I've never seen so much food

414
00:27:39,780 --> 00:27:40,777
What?

415
00:27:40,860 --> 00:27:42,580
Give it back! Now!

416
00:27:43,260 --> 00:27:45,920
They need it more than we do, you morons!

417
00:27:46,220 --> 00:27:48,820
Don't you dare let
Odin's family go hungry!

418
00:27:49,100 --> 00:27:51,453
Put that back on their ship immediately!

419
00:27:51,580 --> 00:27:55,000
I won't say it twice!
Yes, sir! Right away!

420
00:28:00,660 --> 00:28:02,220
Goodbye, Lord Odin!

421
00:28:06,020 --> 00:28:07,360
Goodbye, everyone!

422
00:28:09,100 --> 00:28:10,060
I'll be back!

423
00:28:11,740 --> 00:28:14,269
You better make all of
us proud, all right?

424
00:28:15,040 --> 00:28:15,870
Get yourself!

425
00:28:15,953 --> 00:28:17,024
Can't wait to hear the stories!

426
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:19,440
Have fun up there! See ya!

427
00:28:19,860 --> 00:28:21,480
Be safe, all of you!

428
00:28:32,580 --> 00:28:35,600
It was the second act
of my life as a pirate.

429
00:28:35,980 --> 00:28:37,800
A new adventure had begun.

430
00:28:39,340 --> 00:28:43,800
White Kashi is a great man,
but Roger is remarkable, too.

431
00:28:44,820 --> 00:28:47,220
I'm lucky to have met them both!

432
00:28:51,360 --> 00:28:54,460
Oh, what a sweet little pea you are.

433
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:56,260
Whoopsie-doodle.

434
00:28:57,520 --> 00:29:00,220
I haven't held a baby in a long time.

435
00:29:00,620 --> 00:29:03,500
You know, it reminds me of the old days.

436
00:29:04,840 --> 00:29:06,880
Momonosuke and Hiyori, huh?

437
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:12,500
Ah, baby. My cat smiles.

438
00:29:13,120 --> 00:29:13,950
Wee!

439
00:29:14,033 --> 00:29:14,863
That's my girl.

440
00:29:19,520 --> 00:29:21,180
Captain Roger, sir!

441
00:29:21,480 --> 00:29:23,200
We got a stowaway!

442
00:29:24,780 --> 00:29:25,610
Whoa!

443
00:29:26,220 --> 00:29:27,050
Oh, no!

444
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:30,420
Dog Storm!

445
00:29:30,880 --> 00:29:32,120
Cat Viper!

446
00:29:34,020 --> 00:29:35,680
Why are you here?

447
00:29:36,020 --> 00:29:37,137
Well, why not?

448
00:29:37,220 --> 00:29:41,279
We figured we'd have more fun being
with you, Karoo, on your travels.

449
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:43,616
The dog and the cat have disappeared!

450
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:45,120
Damn it!

451
00:29:45,300 --> 00:29:46,160
Those two!

452
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:55,757
Listen, the only reason you're here is
because you can decipher those poneglyphs.

453
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:57,520
Nothing more, understand?

454
00:30:02,520 --> 00:30:04,680
Next up, I need radishes!

455
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:06,840
Thief, get back here!

456
00:30:07,220 --> 00:30:09,220
Oh, captain's gonna kick his butt.

457
00:30:12,080 --> 00:30:14,200
Odin, don't mess with the locals!

458
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:16,504
I need to get more ingredients.

459
00:30:16,900 --> 00:30:18,724
Just what do you need them for?

460
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:26,520
You see the balls on this guy?

461
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:33,040
Wait, are we in a lawless land?

462
00:30:33,340 --> 00:30:35,697
Are you seeing this, Skobod? I am.

463
00:30:35,780 --> 00:30:38,500
So they aren't civilians, after all.

464
00:30:52,440 --> 00:30:53,270
Odin!

465
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:55,287
Did that really just happen?

466
00:30:57,220 --> 00:30:58,050
Odin!

467
00:31:12,720 --> 00:31:14,180
Holy crap!

468
00:31:15,560 --> 00:31:16,800
You're okay!

469
00:31:17,280 --> 00:31:18,400
That was awesome!

470
00:31:19,820 --> 00:31:24,017
So, I guess since they're not civilians...

471
00:31:24,100 --> 00:31:25,580
They're fair game.

472
00:31:27,040 --> 00:31:28,400
Are you ready?

473
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:30,140
Indeed.

474
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:36,917
I still need some cow, what's it for?

475
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:39,200
To make a delicious broth.

476
00:31:44,380 --> 00:31:50,897
Here a weirdo, all right, enough
of that mess—these guys up!

477
00:31:50,980 --> 00:31:51,810
up

478
00:32:00,140 --> 00:32:01,340
Go, Odin, go!

479
00:32:01,780 --> 00:32:03,360
Go, Odin, go!

480
00:32:04,280 --> 00:32:06,160
Reddish and fried tofu.

481
00:32:07,680 --> 00:32:10,220
Some fish, cakes, and eggs, too.

482
00:32:11,700 --> 00:32:13,560
One, two, and three.

483
00:32:14,020 --> 00:32:15,520
Eat it up for me.

484
00:32:16,300 --> 00:32:18,380
Don't let the whole pot spoil.

485
00:32:19,680 --> 00:32:22,880
I'm old and born to boil.

486
00:32:30,800 --> 00:32:31,630
Hmm?

487
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:34,220
Are you not feeling well? I'm fine.

488
00:32:34,420 --> 00:32:35,773
Nothing to worry about.

489
00:32:35,900 --> 00:32:38,217
What do you mean, nothing to worry about?

490
00:32:38,300 --> 00:32:41,241
Best-case scenario, he's
got a year or so to live.

491
00:32:43,800 --> 00:32:46,820
Gotta catch the wind in
my sails while I can.

492
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:52,220
Here goes!

493
00:32:52,520 --> 00:32:54,461
That's the knock-up stream ahead!

494
00:33:04,820 --> 00:33:06,240
We're dead!

495
00:33:22,480 --> 00:33:23,860
An island?

496
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:28,400
No way!

497
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:35,140
The Sky Island!

498
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:38,340
We gladly welcome you,
people from the Blue Sea!

499
00:33:43,300 --> 00:33:46,740
The world is so much
faster than I had imagined.

500
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:51,141
Not even the gods could have
predicted people living in the clouds!

501
00:34:00,140 --> 00:34:03,300
That fool takes ten
years to master a waiver.

502
00:34:12,200 --> 00:34:14,160
Run for your lives!

503
00:34:25,720 --> 00:34:26,720
This is it!

504
00:34:26,900 --> 00:34:29,860
The City of Gold, Shandora! Wow.

505
00:34:31,200 --> 00:34:32,620
I found it!

506
00:34:33,440 --> 00:34:34,920
All the way up here!

507
00:34:41,200 --> 00:34:42,440
That must be it.

508
00:34:42,800 --> 00:34:44,380
Shandora's Grand Belfry.

509
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:46,580
That thing's pure gold!

510
00:34:46,820 --> 00:34:48,637
How do we haul it back, Captain?

511
00:34:48,720 --> 00:34:49,840
No time for that.

512
00:34:50,220 --> 00:34:53,517
Tell you what, you can come get
it when you're a captain yourself.

513
00:34:53,600 --> 00:34:54,718
Sound good, Boogie?

514
00:34:55,540 --> 00:34:57,952
Can we break off a little piece at least?

515
00:34:58,480 --> 00:35:02,397
The voice is echoing within the
stoner's throng, so it was easy to find.

516
00:35:02,480 --> 00:35:04,900
It's speaking of a great power, isn't it?

517
00:35:14,220 --> 00:35:18,360
The inscription tells you a weapon
named Poseidon. Interesting.

518
00:35:20,380 --> 00:35:24,027
Odin, you're able to write in
this script as well, aren't you?

519
00:35:24,200 --> 00:35:25,500
Yes, of course.

520
00:35:26,900 --> 00:35:28,020
Carve this message!

521
00:35:37,360 --> 00:35:40,737
It's hard to believe Roger is
nearing the end of his life.

522
00:35:40,820 --> 00:35:43,349
He carries on this
quest with such urgency.

523
00:35:43,460 --> 00:35:45,872
I must help him see it to its conclusion.

524
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:49,118
Like this, Captain!

525
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:52,377
That should do it! Nice work.

526
00:35:52,460 --> 00:35:54,060
I made it here,

527
00:35:54,220 --> 00:35:58,237
and I will guide this passage all the
way to the farthest ends of the world.

528
00:35:58,320 --> 00:36:00,840
The stormiest seas will not stop me.

529
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:13,240
I must see it, Raja.

530
00:36:13,840 --> 00:36:18,240
Show me the final chapter of the
adventure you've devoted your life to.

531
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:30,300
Well, boys, let's go back
to the blue scene! Yeah!
